---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Ice Hockey Shifts: Privacy"
  description="Privacy policy for the Ice Hockey Shifts iPhone app."
  alternate="/fr/iceshifts/confidentialite/">
  <section class="top narrow prose">
    <p class="meta kicker">Ice Hockey Shifts</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated 2026-11-13 · <a href="/fr/iceshifts/confidentialite/" hreflang="fr">Français</a></p>

    <p>Ice Hockey Shifts (the phone app) is made by Matthew Macri, an individual developer in Montréal,
    Québec. This policy explains what the app does with your information. In short: <strong>without an
    account, nothing leaves your phone.</strong> An account is optional; if you create one, your games are
    kept on a server in Montréal so they can follow you to another phone and, once Garmin allows it, arrive
    from Garmin Connect by themselves.</p>

    <p>There is no advertising, no analytics, no tracking and no artificial intelligence in the app or on
    the server. Your information is never sold or rented.</p>

    <h2>Without an account</h2>
    <p>The app reads activity files (<code>.fit</code>, or a <code>.zip</code> containing them) that you choose
    to open in it, usually exported from Garmin Connect after a game recorded with the Ice Hockey Shifts watch
    app. Imported games, the original files and your settings (position and how many players were dressed)
    are stored only on your phone, inside the app's own storage. Like other app data, they may be included
    in your device's iCloud or computer backup, depending on your backup settings. Nothing is sent to the
    developer or anyone else.</p>

    <h2>With an account</h2>
    <p>Accounts are available from version 1.1 of the app. You sign in with Apple; there is no password.
    When you are signed in, the app and the server keep the following.</p>

    <h3>What is kept, and why</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account identity.</strong> The identifier Apple gives this app for your Apple Account, and
      the email address Apple shares (often a private relay address if you choose "Hide My Email"). Used
      only to recognise your account. We do not send you marketing email.</li>
      <li><strong>Games recorded with Ice Hockey Shifts.</strong> For each game: its start time and length,
      laps and shifts, per-second heart rate and the respiration-rate estimate your watch records, your
      heart-rate zone settings and maximum heart rate, stride-based distance if your watch records one, and
      the watch model and software version. Used to show you your games and to keep them in step between
      your phones. Activities recorded by other apps are never uploaded; they stay on your phone.</li>
      <li><strong>Your answers.</strong> Your position, and how many players were dressed for each game.</li>
      <li><strong>Sign-in sessions.</strong> A random token per signed-in phone, stored on the server only as
      a one-way hash.</li>
      <li><strong>Garmin Connect link</strong>, only if you connect it: your Garmin user ID, the access tokens
      Garmin issues (encrypted on the server) and the permissions you granted.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What is removed before anything is sent</h3>
    <p>A watch's activity file also contains your Garmin profile (weight, height, gender, resting heart
    rate, sleep and wake times), device settings such as your time zone, and the serial numbers of your
    watch and the devices paired with it. The app does not use these, so it blanks them in the copy it
    uploads, and the server does the same to anything Garmin sends. They are not stored. Games recorded
    with Ice Hockey Shifts contain no GPS location.</p>

    <h3>Where it is kept</h3>
    <p>On a server operated by the developer in Montréal, Québec, Canada, in a database on that server.
    The account and its games are not copied anywhere else. Connections to the server pass through
    Cloudflare, a network provider that protects the website and may handle requests in other countries,
    including the United States. The server tells Cloudflare not to keep copies of its answers.</p>

    <h3>Service providers</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Apple</strong> handles Sign in with Apple and tells the app who you are.</li>
      <li><strong>Garmin</strong>, only if you connect Garmin Connect: Garmin sends the server the games
      recorded with Ice Hockey Shifts after your watch syncs. Garmin's own privacy policy applies to the
      data Garmin holds.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> carries the connection between the app and the server.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>None of them receives your games from us. Data from Garmin is not shared with anyone else.</p>

    <h3>How long it is kept</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Games and answers: until you remove the game or delete your account. When you remove a game, its
      data and file are deleted at once; only its identifier and the time of removal are kept, so that your
      other phones remove it too. These are deleted with the account.</li>
      <li>Sign-in sessions: until you sign out on that phone, or 180 days after you signed in on it.</li>
      <li>Garmin link: until you disconnect it in the app or in Garmin Connect, or delete your account. If
      you withdraw the app's access in Garmin Connect, games that came from Garmin are deleted.</li>
      <li>Server logs record the time, the type of request and whether it worked, without your IP address.
      The web server in front of it keeps IP addresses for 14 days for security, then deletes them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Deleting your account</h3>
    <p>In the app: Settings, Account, Delete account. This deletes the account, every game and answer
    stored in it and the Garmin link, immediately. The games on your phone stay. You can also ask by
    email (below).</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask to see the information kept about you, to get a copy of it in a common format, to
    correct it, or to have it deleted, and you can withdraw your consent at any time by deleting your
    account. Write to the person in charge of personal information below; you will get an answer within
    30 days. If you are not satisfied, you may complain to the Commission d'accès à l'information du Québec
    or the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada.</p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>Connections are encrypted (HTTPS). Garmin tokens are encrypted on the server, sign-in tokens are
    stored only as hashes, and the session token on your phone is kept in the iOS keychain. No system is
    perfectly secure; if a breach put your information at risk of serious harm, you and the Commission
    d'accès à l'information would be told.</p>

    <h2>Health information</h2>
    <p>Heart-rate figures are shown for training interest only. The app is not a medical device and does
    not give medical advice.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Accounts are meant for people 14 and older. A younger player may use the app without an account,
    which sends nothing anywhere; an account for a child under 14 needs a parent's consent.</p>

    <h2>Person in charge of personal information</h2>
    <p>Matthew Macri, <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page with a new date.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
